<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20591] Support iterating OSD objects via llapi</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20591</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;It will be very useful if we can do that for some obvious reasons:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Better policy engine - it can just iterate the objects on the MDTs to make a decision which files should be moved&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Rebalance OSTs - by iterating objects on fully occupied OSTs, it can figure out which large objects should be migrated, especially with this proposed &lt;a href="https://wiki.whamcloud.com/spaces/PUB/pages/479428774/Stripe+Replacement+Phase+0" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;feature&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The work seems straightforward. I will burn some tokens and get some patches.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
